WEBVTT

00:50:28.286 --> 00:50:30.548
That's an act of great courage.

00:50:30.572 --> 00:50:33.093
And with that act of courage,
you create combustion,

00:50:33.117 --> 00:50:34.675
you create emotional combustion.

00:50:34.699 --> 00:50:36.533
And that's how communities are formed.

00:50:36.557 --> 00:50:38.160
I think most of us know that,

00:50:38.184 --> 00:50:41.084
but there's a group of people
who are not weavers of society,

00:50:41.108 --> 00:50:42.417
who are rippers of society,

00:50:42.441 --> 00:50:46.283
and when they see vulnerability,
they see a chance to pounce and destroy.

00:50:46.307 --> 00:50:50.297
And I don't know what they're
acting out of, but it is a fact.

00:50:50.321 --> 00:50:53.102
But that doesn't mean
vulnerability should be stopped.

00:50:53.126 --> 00:50:56.049
Brené Brown, a woman
I don't know, but I admire her,

00:50:56.073 --> 00:50:57.997
she's written a lot about vulnerability,

00:50:58.021 --> 00:51:01.234
and I think she's correctly identified
the key trait of our age.